      ],
      "summary": "Founded in 2008, 350.org is a global climate advocacy organization that mobilizes communities to challenge systems causing environmental degradation through training and public campaigns <cite id=\"5\">focused on climate solutions</cite>. In FY2024, the organization operated with a <cite id=\"6\">total revenue of $19,587,115</cite> while executing international initiatives across direct community training, fossil fuel divestment, and renewable energy policy advocacy. The organization maintains <cite id=\"7\">a 97/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite> and holds a <cite id=\"5\">Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite>. Financial filings show a <cite id=\"6\">program expense ratio of 81.5%</cite> in FY2024, allocating the clear majority of its operational expenditures directly toward advocacy and movement-building programs. As an advocacy-focused entity, its model prioritizes systemic policy change and capacity building rather than traditional direct relief, offering sadaqah-eligible donors a vehicle for global environmental policy engagement.",
